\title{Semidirect product}
\author{brentyorgey}
\date{2026-01-09T15:24:33Z}
\taxon{Definition}

\p{Let #{S} and #{A} be [semigroups](0033), with #{A} [acting](0035) [distributively](0038) on #{S}. Then the \em{semidirect product} #{S \rtimes A} is the set #{S \times A} together with the binary operation ##{(s_1, a_1) \diamond (s_2, a_2) = (s_1(a_1 \cdot s_2), a_1a_2).}}
